---
title: Hot and Sour Soup
description: Well-known soup from Peking gains its hotness from very liberal use of ground pepper
source: The Chinese Kitchen <urn:isbn:9781856267021>
author: Deh-Ta Hsiung
course: Starter
servings: 4
prep time: 20m
cook time: 15m
locale: en_GB
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: Chinese
tags:
- meat
- savoury
- poultry
- soup
- chinese
- starter
---

Squeeze dry the @dried Chinese mushrooms{4}(soaked) and discard any hard stalks. Thinly shred the mushrooms, @pork or chicken meat, raw or cooked{115%g}, @sliced bamboo shoots{50%g}(rinsed and drained) and @tofu (bean curd){150%g}.

Bring the @./Savoury/Chinese Clear Stock{900%ml} to a rolling boil. Stir in the mushrooms, meat, bamboo shoots and bean curd. Bring back to the boil and add the @rice wine{1%tbsp}, @light soy sauce{1%tbsp}, @rice vinegar{1%tbsp} and @ground white pepper{1%tsp}. Bring back to the boil once more and pour the @egg{1}(lightly beaten) very slowly into the soup, stirring at the same time.

Gently stir in the @cornflour paste{1%tbsp} to thicken the soup. Add the @salt{1%tsp} and @?monosodium glutamate{}, if using, and serve hot garnished with the @spring onions{}(finely chopped).